<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Second Anglo-Afghan War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1878">1878</a>–<a href="/years/1880">1880</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Second Anglo-Afghan War was fought from 1878 to 1880 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, after the emir Sher Ali Khan received a Russian mission. British forces occupied much of the country and imposed the Treaty of Gandamak in 1879, but the murder of the British envoy in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kabul">Kabul</a> and the defeat at Maiwand prolonged the war. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> withdrew after recognising <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdur-rahman-khan">Abdur Rahman Khan</a> as emir, keeping control of Afghan foreign policy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/second-anglo-afghan-war.jpg" alt="Second Anglo-Afghan War" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AfghanTsakhtan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:9th_Regiment_at_Ali_Masjid.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
